message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "DOUBLE JEOPARDY: The Vulnerability Spiral — Compound Climate Risk Across Five Island Nations"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Maske"
    given-names: "Sakshi D."
repository-code: "https://github.com/sakshimaske303-commits/DOUBLE-JEOPARDY"
url: "https://github.com/sakshimaske303-commits/DOUBLE-JEOPARDY"
abstract: >-
  This geospatial analysis examines climate vulnerability across five island
  nations (Maldives, Lakshadweep, Seychelles, Fiji, Canary Islands) by
  analyzing physical exposure to sea-level rise and degradation of natural
  coastal defenses independently. The project combines settlement-level
  elevation data, mangrove extent tracking (1996, 2010, 2020), and 24-year
  coral bleaching records. Key findings reveal statistically significant
  coral bleaching stress trends in the Maldives and Seychelles, stable
  mangrove coverage across all islands, and a Compound Vulnerability Score
  showing highest risk in Seychelles despite the Maldives having the
  greatest physical exposure (99.1% of settlements at risk).
keywords:
  - sea-level rise
  - mangroves
  - coral bleaching
  - compound vulnerability
  - small island developing states
  - protected-area effectiveness
  - remote sensing
  - climate adaptation
  - geospatial analysis
